{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Rich-text DC PIVOT — all 4 de-risking experiments PASSED (parallel subagents; scripts+reports in session files/).\n1) Echo-suppression+LWW: n=800; self-echo 0 spurious re-syncs / 0 local rewrites; concurrent edits 799/799 conflicts DETECTED, 0 silently destroyed; norm() masks 0 real changes. CRITICAL AC: baseline = value OBSERVED AFTER push (Jira's canonical form), not raw wire sent → +1 GET per changed field. One-way design means never inb() in echo path (adversarial out∘inb 32.7% drift is upper bound only).\n2) Repo-cost (epic-0303 methodology): change-gated rich_sha=sha256(wire)[:16] (8 bytes) INLINE in bindings.json = 0.07 KB/ver stable, identical to baseline; per-pass timestamp anti-pattern reproduced 0303's 12.79→12.62 KB. Respects churn discipline; full-wire storage rejected.\n3) Cross-project generalization: safety perfect+invariant across 23 env_ids/6 authors + OOD cli/cli(489); 0 corruptions; coverage 68.2% bodies/78.5% chars, authors CV<6.4%, OOD over-performs → not overfit. Future guard candidate: OOD HTML density ~30×.\n4) Live-oracle: draft test extends existing Docker DC harness (renderedFields HTML fidelity, not just REST source); offline checks pass; live gap (Jira canonicalization/renderer) scoped to jira-dc-harness CI job. IMPL AC: arrow substitution runs on MD BEFORE pandoc.\nVERDICT: pivot fully validated. Next: author epic (depends on 0303/e369/3e73). Open decision: comment edit/delete semantics (append-only vs full sync via persistent Jira-comment-ID map)."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785798846252719001,"uuid":"2e91855c-387c-4428-8d9c-d4ae68d5ce9b"}